# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 serving window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of serving/tp4-s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled
# in by whoever drives the window; every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image and its stop rule.
# A POST-EVIDENCE job: image tp4-serve-2, built from the commit that records packed_any_evidence_tp4.json (the record is baked into
# the image, so the image is built AFTER it), serving c2-packed-tp4, the TRAFFIC profile and the image default: the attach is
# admitted by the record and a missing or stale record is a refusal, never a fallback.
# SR (TP2 M12, G7): the four-card platform replay: the agent's serving sequence on all four boards (resolved at run time: none
# named) in a copy of its container running the THIN LAYER image (sha256:7ecbd834bcb71f5b55057044620a023eca221cf8720dd819fbb6ee0ab6b045ad: the platform image built on tp4-serve-2 and
# pre-pulled into the rig daemon, given by digest). C2_REPLAY_PROFILE is the four-card traffic profile the copy must BOOT by the
# image default: the agent forwards no QWEN_C2_PROFILE, so the replay sets none either; the served model is left at its default,
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt. Each boot's (load, reload, restart) vLLM subprocess log - the runtime's /tmp/thatch_vllm_N.log, read from
# the container, never docker logs - must show '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh line, admission
# passed with no UNQUALIFIED, parser M armed, 'extent replay engaged' and the prefill warm checks; the n=2 edge refusal is judged
# strictly because the contract line is read from that log. The source record's image must be present in the rig daemon (the
# replay subtracts its ENV; without it the replay refuses before docker run). The restart step (docker stop with the teardown skipped, then
# docker start) is the first reopening of the four-card mesh after an unclean exit: a wedge there FAILS the replay and blocks
# placement; the next job must then begin with the quad reset and heal.
# Duration (estimate): 25-35 min, then a quad reset (a one-action quad job) and the platform's fabric re-measure. Stop rule: any FAIL stops placement.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-3
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=sha256:7ecbd834bcb71f5b55057044620a023eca221cf8720dd819fbb6ee0ab6b045ad
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
